+**§6.6:** "**Shift+Slip** (motor toggle) and anything else in the manual that touches the motor."
+
+| nn · file | Prompt | Expected |
+|---|---|---|
+| `31-motor-toggle` | Deck 1: press Shift+Slip, wait 5 s, Shift+Slip again, wait 5 s. Deck 2: the same. Then, with a motor running, flip the rear torque switch to the other position and back. Note anything the platter did. Enter when done. | 1.0 min |
+
+**§6.7:** "**Strip search / needle-drop** if present: touch at several positions, release."
+
+| nn · file | Prompt | Expected |
+|---|---|---|
+| `32-strip` | If the One has a strip search / needle drop (press s to skip if not): on each deck touch it at the left end, the middle and the right end, 1 s each, then slide along it once. Enter when done. | 0.75 min |
+
+Deck 2's recordings use deck 1's prompt with "Deck 2" in place of "Deck 1" and the same expected time:
+`12-hand-d2-slow` 0.5 · `13-hand-d2-fast` 0.25 · `14-hand-d2-ten` 0.75 · `15-hand-d2-touch` 0.25 ·
+`16-hand-d2-alt` 0.5 (2.25 min), and `23-motor-d2-33` 1.25 · `24-motor-d2-45` 1.4 · `25-motor-d2-hold` 0.3 ·
+`26-motor-d2-backspin` 0.3 · `27-motor-d2-stop-min` 0.35 · `28-motor-d2-stop-max` 0.5 (4.1 min).
+
+**Totals:** §6.1 1.0 · §6.2 11.5 · §6.3 4.5 · §6.4 8.2 · §6.5 1.2 · §6.6 1.0 · §6.7 0.75 = **28.15 min** of
+steps, plus about 5 min of setup that is not a step. That is **over** the 25 min of M2-06 step 2 and M2-07 step 1.
+The census times are honest estimates: pads ≈ 8 modes × 8 pads, with and without Shift, at ≈ 1 s a press; each
+deck's ≈ 20 buttons × 2 at ≈ 1.7 s for press, hold 1 s and release, plus knob sweeps. Squeezing them to fit would
+mislead Michael at the controller. **D15 *default*:** keep §6 whole, time it at ≈ 28 min, and let `--list` print
+the honest total. The question to Michael is whether to raise the cap to 30 min or cut something (proposed cut if
+he wants 25: pads with Shift in one mode only, −2 min; the 45 step to 30 s, −1 min). `--list` prints the 7 groups
+with these per-group times and the total, then the 32 files.
+
+Tests (`tests/capture-session.test.mjs`, M2-06) run with scripted stdin and `--capture-cmd <stub>`, where the stub
+writes one fixed JSONL line and records its arguments, or with `--device <fifo>`. They check one file per step,
+that `r` overwrites, that `s` writes `skipped`, the README lines, that an existing directory is refused without
+`--resume`, the `--list` total, and the power-off/Enter/power-on wording and the align/ten-turns wording.
+
+**As built (M2-06):**
+- **Numbering and extras (D17 *default*):** the main session is `01-power-on` … `26-strip`, 24.75 min in the 7
+  groups. The order is §6.1 `01`, §6.2 `02`–`06`, §6.3 deck 1 `07`–`11` (slow, fast, ten, touch, alt) and deck 2
+  `12`–`14` (slow, ten, touch), §6.4 deck 1 `15`–`20` and deck 2 `21`–`22` (33, 45), §6.5 `23`–`24`, §6.6 `25` and
+  §6.7 `26`. Optional extras come after it, each skippable with `s`, 4.40 min in all: `27`/`28-census-d<n>-pads-shift`
+  (Shift pads in every mode but the first), `29-hand-d2-fast`, `30-hand-d2-alt`, `31-motor-d2-hold`,
+  `32-motor-d2-backspin`, `33-motor-d2-stop-min` and `34-motor-d2-stop-max`. The main pad steps keep each mode
+  unshifted plus Shift in the first mode (1.4 min each). The 45 step rings its bell at 5 s and 65 s. The hold step
+  starts the motor itself if it isn't running. `23-pitch-d1` says to stop deck 2's motor first.
+- **Input:** each answer is a line (Enter, `s`, `r` or `k`). A line typed while a recording runs stops it, timed
+  steps included. At a terminal, keys pressed before a question is shown are dropped, so an extra Enter can't
+  answer "keep" unseen. Piped input is a script, so the tests' lines all count. A take with 0 messages needs `k`
+  to be kept. A stop waits until the capture has created its output file (or 2 s have passed). tools/capture
+  installs its SIGINT handler before it creates the file, so an early stop can't kill it before the take exists.
+  End of input exits 1, telling you to resume with `--resume`.
+- **Takes:** each attempt records to `<nn>-<step>.jsonl.part`, which `*.jsonl` globs (census) don't pick up. It is
+  renamed to `.jsonl` only when kept, and tools/capture is never given `--force`. A take interrupted by Ctrl-C
+  stays as `.part`; `--resume` shows its message count and offers it for review (Enter keeps it, `r`
+  re-records). A capture that fails after recording something (exit 1, "device gone") offers `k` to keep the
+  partial take, marked `partial: capture exit 1` in README.
+- **Power-on:** the port must leave `amidi -l` within 30 s of Enter. If it doesn't (a standby that keeps USB
+  alive), the tool asks Michael to leave the One off and unplug its USB cable, then waits 30 s more. Only once
+  the port is gone does it record with `--wait 60 --seconds 10`, saying "don't press Enter: it cancels". If the
+  port never goes away, the attempt fails and is offered again; it is never recorded with the port still there.
+- **Resume after midnight:** with `--resume` and no session for today, the newest `<date>-<label>` is resumed.
+- **README:** the header holds the date, `git rev-parse --short HEAD`, `Port: <name> = hw:…` (or "not listed by
+  amidi -l at the start", or `Device: <path>`) and the setup note. After it comes `## Steps`, with lines in session
+  order (lines for files not in the step list, from an older numbering, are kept after them). The message count
+  comes from the take's file. The seconds come from capture's summary line (wall time if
+  there is none), plus `dropped <n>` when the parser dropped bytes. On `--resume` the header is kept as it is.
+- **Options for tests:** `--capture-cmd <cmd>` (a stub given capture's arguments) and `--captures-dir <dir>`.
+  `--device <path>` skips the power-on port watch: there is no name to watch.
+- `amidi -l` parsing moved to `tools/lib/amidi.mjs`, which tools/capture now uses too.
+
+**Live use is Michael's, staged** (so `HARDWARE-TESTS.md` copies it):
+1. Dry run with no hardware involved: `tools/capture-session --list` shows the 7 groups, 24.75 min, and the
+   extras, 4.40 min (D17).
+2. A 5 s check with the One on and Mixxx closed: `tools/capture --port 'Rane ONE MIDI 1' --seconds 5 --out
+   /tmp/check.jsonl`, wiggling one knob. The file should have `cc` lines. Exit 5 means another program holds the
+   port: close it.
+3. The full session: `tools/capture-session --label census`. If a step goes wrong, press `r`. If the tool breaks
+   mid-session, `tools/capture-session --label census --resume` continues where it stopped.
+Undo: delete `captures/<date>-census/` before committing. Nothing else changes.
+
+## HARDWARE-TESTS outline
+
+M2-07 writes `HARDWARE-TESTS.md` at the repo root. Its sections and what each holds:
+
+- **Before you start:** a tape mark on each platter edge and one on the chassis next to it. The known positions
+  from the session's opening prompt (faders, knobs, pitch centre, 33). Motor off, both platters still. Source
+  selectors on USB. Mixxx, Serato and anything else using the One closed. The checkout on the branch to commit to.
